export default function Page2(){return <><Frame0 /><main><div className={"scroll-progress custom-article-progress"} data-scroll-progress={"#ag4-article-text"} aria-hidden={"true"}></div><section id={"ag4-page-head"} className={"custom-ph custom-article-head relative isolate overflow-x-clip"} aria-labelledby={"ag4-page-title"}><div className={"container"}><div className={"custom-head"}><nav aria-label={"Breadcrumb"} data-anim={"fade-up"}><ol className={"custom-query custom-query--tone-2 custom-ph-crumbs flex-wrap"}><li><a href={"#page=demo-seo-agency-1"}>{"Home"}</a></li><li><a href={"#page=demo-seo-agency-1-insights"}>{"Insights"}</a></li><li aria-current={"page"}>{"AI Search"}</li></ol></nav><h1 id={"ag4-page-title"} className={"custom-display text-[clamp(2.25rem,1.4rem_+_3.5vw,4.25rem)]"} data-anim={"blur-up"}>{"How to get cited in AI answers: "}<span className={"font-semibold"}>{"what 400 prompts taught us."}</span></h1><p className={"custom-voice-by"} data-anim={"fade-up"}><img src={"https://draftmango.com/framo/assets/media/placeholder/160x160.svg"} alt={""} width={"56"} height={"56"} decoding={"async"} loading={"lazy"} /><strong>{"Nadia Ferrer"}</strong><span>{"Strategy Lead · "}<time datetime={"2026-10-06"}>{"Oct 6, 2026"}</time>{" · 9 Min Read"}</span></p></div><img className={"w-full aspect-[2/1] mt-[clamp(2.5rem,5vw,4.5rem)] object-cover rounded-(--custom-radius) max-md:aspect-[4/3]"} src={"https://draftmango.com/framo/assets/media/placeholder/2000x1125.svg"} alt={"Nadia Ferrer at a window desk, an answer card with three source chips on her laptop"} width={"2000"} height={"1125"} decoding={"async"} fetchPriority={"high"} data-anim={"fade-up"} data-anim-delay={"150"} /></div></section><section id={"ag4-article-body"} className={"custom-section"} aria-label={"Article"}><div className={"container"}><article id={"ag4-article-text"} className={"article-body custom-article-text px-0 text-[clamp(1.0625rem,1rem_+_0.3vw,1.1875rem)] leading-[1.7]"}><p className={"font-heading text-[clamp(1.3125rem,1.2rem_+_0.6vw,1.625rem)] leading-[1.42] tracking-[-0.012em] text-text text-pretty"}>{"For six months we asked three answer engines the same 400 buying questions every week and logged every source they named. The pattern that came back is plainer than the hype suggests, and most of it is work you already know how to do."}</p><h2 className={"font-medium tracking-[-0.022em] text-[clamp(1.75rem,1.45rem_+_1.2vw,2.375rem)]"}>{"Why the citation is the new click"}</h2><p>{"In 2019, 62 of every 100 searches in our client panel ended on a classic result. In 2026 it is 34. Another 27 end on an answer, and 39 end with no click at all."}</p><figure className={"custom-panel custom-panel--tone-4 custom-shift-panel custom-article-figure grid gap-4 pt-(--custom-gutter) pb-4.5 px-(--custom-gutter) max-w-184"} data-anim={"fade-up"}><span className={"custom-lozenge"} aria-hidden={"true"}></span><div className={"custom-card grid gap-[clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2.25rem)] text-text"}><p className={"font-heading text-[1.375rem] font-semibold leading-[1.25] tracking-[-0.015em]"}>{"Where 100 Searches End"}</p><dl className={"grid grid-cols-[auto_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-4 items-center"}><dt className={"font-heading text-[1.125rem] font-medium tabular-nums"}>{"2019"}</dt><dd className={"custom-shift-bar flex gap-1 h-13"} role={"img"} aria-label={"2019: 62 in 100 searches ended on a classic result, 9 on an answer and 29 without a click"}><span className={"custom-shift-seg custom-shift-seg--links [--seg:62]"}>{"62"}</span><span className={"custom-shift-seg custom-shift-seg--answers [--seg:9]"}>{"9"}</span><span className={"custom-shift-seg custom-shift-seg--none [--seg:29]"}>{"29"}</span></dd><dt className={"font-heading text-[1.125rem] font-medium tabular-nums"}>{"2026"}</dt><dd className={"custom-shift-bar flex gap-1 h-13"} role={"img"} aria-label={"2026: 34 in 100 searches ended on a classic result, 27 on an answer and 39 without a click"}><span className={"custom-shift-seg custom-shift-seg--links [--seg:34]"}>{"34"}</span><span className={"custom-shift-seg custom-shift-seg--answers [--seg:27]"}>{"27"}</span><span className={"custom-shift-seg custom-shift-seg--none [--seg:39]"}>{"39"}</span></dd></dl><ul className={"custom-shift-legend flex flex-wrap gap-y-2 gap-x-6 text-[0.9375rem] leading-[1.4] text-soft"} role={"list"}><li className={"custom-shift-seg--links inline-flex gap-2 items-center"}>{"Classic Results"}</li><li className={"custom-shift-seg--answers inline-flex gap-2 items-center mt-0"}>{"Answers"}</li><li className={"custom-shift-seg--none inline-flex gap-2 items-center mt-0"}>{"No Click"}</li></ul></div><figcaption className={"custom-shift-source px-4 text-start"}>{"Source: Framo client panel, 2026"}</figcaption></figure><p>{"The demand did not go anywhere. People still ask. They read the reply above the results and move on. When that reply names you, you have been recommended before anyone compared tabs. When it names a rival, the comparison is over before it starts."}</p><h2 className={"font-medium tracking-[-0.022em] text-[clamp(1.75rem,1.45rem_+_1.2vw,2.375rem)]"}>{"What we tracked"}</h2><p>{"The 400 prompts came from 22 clients in software, retail and healthcare. Each one was a question a buyer would really ask: which tool suits a team of ten, what a fair price looks like, who is open late nearby. We ran the set every week and recorded three things: whether the client was named, whether its page was cited as a source, and which other sources stood beside it."}</p><p>{"An answer cited "}<strong>{"four sources on average."}</strong>{" That is the whole shelf. There is no position eleven to be patient in."}</p><h2 className={"font-medium tracking-[-0.022em] text-[clamp(1.75rem,1.45rem_+_1.2vw,2.375rem)]"}>{"Three things the cited pages share"}</h2><ol><li><strong>{"They rank already."}</strong>{" Of the pages that were cited, 71% also sat in the top ten organic results for the same question. Answer engines lean on the pages search already trusts, so classic SEO is the entry ticket, not the old way."}</li><li className={"mt-3.5"}><strong>{"They answer first."}</strong>{" Pages that gave a direct answer within their first 60 words were cited 2.3 times as often as pages that opened with background."}</li><li className={"mt-3.5"}><strong>{"They are specific."}</strong>{" A price, a number of days, a named limit. Pages with a figure a model could lift were quoted. Pages that stayed general were paraphrased without credit."}</li></ol><blockquote className={"custom-article-quote"}><p>{"An answer engine does not reward the best page. It rewards "}<span className={"font-semibold"}>{"the page that is easiest to quote."}</span></p></blockquote><h2 className={"font-medium tracking-[-0.022em] text-[clamp(1.75rem,1.45rem_+_1.2vw,2.375rem)]"}>{"Mentions matter as much as pages"}</h2><p>{"The surprise was how often a brand was named without its own site being a source. In 38% of the answers that recommended a client, the citation pointed somewhere else: a buyer guide, a comparison, a forum thread. The model had learned the brand from other people's pages."}</p><p>{"That is digital PR doing a job it was never measured on. Coverage that says what you do, in plain words, on sites the engines read, moves how often you are recommended."}</p><h3 className={"font-medium tracking-[-0.022em]"}>{"What did not matter"}</h3><p>{"Three things we expected to count and could not find in the data: page length, publishing frequency, and markup written specially for AI crawlers. Long pages were cited when they answered early and ignored when they did not."}</p><h2 className={"font-medium tracking-[-0.022em] text-[clamp(1.75rem,1.45rem_+_1.2vw,2.375rem)]"}>{"Where to start this month"}</h2><p>{"Pick the twenty questions closest to a sale. Ask them yourself and write down who is named. For each one where you are missing, check whether you rank in the top ten. If you do not, that is the first fix. If you do, rewrite the opening so the answer comes first and carries a figure. Then look at the other sources cited and ask which of them could fairly mention you."}</p><p>{"Run the same twenty again in a month. Lumaway did exactly this with its category question and went from absent to cited first in ten months. It is slower than an advert, and it does not switch off when the budget does."}</p></article><footer className={"custom-article-foot max-w-168 mt-[clamp(3rem,6vw,4.5rem)] mr-auto ml-auto pt-8 border-t border-t-(--custom-line)"}><div className={"social-share"} x-data={"{ copied: false }"}><span className={"social-share-label"}>{"Share This Article"}</span><ul className={"social-list"} role={"list"}><li><button type={"button"} className={"social-link social-link--circle social-link--soft"} {...{"x-bind:aria-label": "copied ? 'Link copied' : 'Copy link'"}} aria-label={"Copy link"} {...{"x-on:click": "navigator.clipboard?.writeText(location.href); copied = true; setTimeout(() => copied = false, 1800)"}}><i className={"ph ph-link"} x-show={"!copied"} aria-hidden={"true"}></i><i className={"ph ph-check"} x-show={"copied"} x-cloak={""} aria-hidden={"true"}></i></button></li><li><a href={"#"} className={"social-link social-link--circle social-link--soft social-link--brand"} data-social={"x"} aria-label={"Share on X"}><i className={"ph ph-x-logo"} aria-hidden={"true"}></i></a></li><li><a href={"#"} className={"social-link social-link--circle social-link--soft social-link--brand"} data-social={"linkedin"} aria-label={"Share on LinkedIn"}><i className={"ph ph-linkedin-logo"} aria-hidden={"true"}></i></a></li><li><a href={"#"} className={"social-link social-link--circle social-link--soft social-link--brand"} data-social={"facebook"} aria-label={"Share on Facebook"}><i className={"ph ph-facebook-logo"} aria-hidden={"true"}></i></a></li><li><a href={"#"} className={"social-link social-link--circle social-link--soft"} aria-label={"Share by email"}><i className={"ph ph-envelope-simple"} aria-h